rownowaznik: "<p>The Wilanów dial gives three readings from a single shadow: equal hours, Italian hours counted from the last sunset, and Babylonian hours counted from sunrise. True solar time at Wilanów never agrees with a mechanical clock — the gap runs between roughly ten and forty minutes across the year. The instrument lets you set a date and a clock reading — or take hold of the sun and move it across the sky — then read the shadow off three separate grids of lines. The sun's position is computed for the leap year 2028, so 29 February is available; across the four-year cycle the same date moves the shadow by less than the width of a drawn line.</p>"
